    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Recurrent sudden episodes of unresponsiveness for two years, two or three a month: he &apos;blanks out&apos;, stops speaking, slumps or sinks to the floor with his eyes closed for two to ten minutes, and afterwards is tearful and tired, with no tongue biting, incontinence, or injury; first during a period of overwork and little sleep at college; with low mood and anxiety; unchanged on levetiracetam; under evaluation for epilepsy, functional (dissociative) seizures, syncope, and other causes</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R40.4</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem echoing his documented overwork, infirm health, and low spirits, and the later accounts of sudden attacks; superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Taking an antiseizure medicine (levetiracetam) started without a confirmed diagnosis of epilepsy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z79.899</td><td>S — Synthetic medication problem for teaching about avoiding unneeded antiseizure medicines; resolved when the medicine was stopped.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

