    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Recurrent sudden episodes of unresponsiveness for two years, two or three a month: he &apos;blanks out&apos;, stops speaking, slumps or sinks to the floor with his eyes closed for two to ten minutes, and afterwards is tearful and tired, with no tongue biting, incontinence, or injury; first during a period of overwork and little sleep at college; with low mood and anxiety; unchanged on levetiracetam; under evaluation for epilepsy, functional (dissociative) seizures, syncope, and other causes: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Taking an antiseizure medicine (levetiracetam) started without a confirmed diagnosis of epilepsy: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

