<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Diagnostic workup: a detailed history including a witness account or phone video if available, ECG, blood count, metabolic panel, TSH, brain MRI with an epilepsy protocol, and inpatient video-EEG monitoring to capture his habitual events; levetiracetam continued unchanged until the evaluation is complete. Guideline: LaFrance WC Jr, et al. Minimum requirements for the diagnosis of psychogenic nonepileptic seizures: a staged approach: a report from the International League Against Epilepsy Nonepileptic Seizures Task Force. Epilepsia 2013;54(11):2005-2018 (PMID 24111933) (2013); Hingray C, et al. Functional/dissociative seizures: Proposal for a new diagnostic label and definition by the ILAE task force. Epilepsia 2025;66(11):4162-4182 (PMID 40884444) (2025); Fisher RS, et al. Operational classification of seizure types by the International League Against Epilepsy. Epilepsia 2017;58(4):522-530 (PMID 28276060) (2017); Fisher RS, et al. ILAE official report: a practical clinical definition of epilepsy. Epilepsia 2014;55(4):475-482 (PMID 24730690) (2014) [S]</item><item>Safety now: no driving until the evaluation is complete and the neurologist advises; showers rather than baths, no swimming alone or working at heights; seizure first aid for the people he lives and works near. Guideline: Tolchin B, et al. Seizures, Driver Licensure, and Medical Reporting Update: An AAN Position Statement. Neurology 2025;104(7):e213459 (PMID 40073306) (2025); First Aid for Seizures (2026) [S]</item><item>Suicide risk assessment with a written safety plan: warning signs, coping steps, people to contact, the clinic number, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline; the rifle locked with the ammunition stored separately; safety reviewed at every visit. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024) [S]</item><item>Neurology consultation (epilepsy and functional neurological disorder) with admission for video-EEG monitoring, on the diagnosis, the antiseizure medicine, and treatment. Guideline: LaFrance WC Jr, et al. Minimum requirements for the diagnosis of psychogenic nonepileptic seizures: a staged approach: a report from the International League Against Epilepsy Nonepileptic Seizures Task Force. Epilepsia 2013;54(11):2005-2018 (PMID 24111933) (2013); Hingray C, et al. Functional/dissociative seizures: Proposal for a new diagnostic label and definition by the ILAE task force. Epilepsia 2025;66(11):4162-4182 (PMID 40884444) (2025); Fisher RS, et al. Operational classification of seizure types by the International League Against Epilepsy. Epilepsia 2017;58(4):522-530 (PMID 28276060) (2017) [S]</item><item>Measurement-based care for depression and anxiety: PHQ-9 and GAD-7 at least monthly during treatment; psychotherapy, an SSRI such as sertraline, or both, by shared decision once the cause of the events is clear. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022) [S]</item><item>Driving: may resume once free of events for at least three months and with the neurologist&apos;s agreement, following state licensing rules and the AAN 2025 position. Guideline: Tolchin B, et al. Seizures, Driver Licensure, and Medical Reporting Update: An AAN Position Statement. Neurology 2025;104(7):e213459 (PMID 40073306) (2025) [S]</item></list></text>

